  "description": "Spec-054 FR-009 — Adversarial mismatch in component (b) payment_payload subset.\n\nThe ReceiptEnvelope is correctly signed (valid JWS, valid kid in JWKS, valid\ntimestamp_evidence) and declares a Permit2 authorization with amount =\n'1000000'. At verify time the auditor is presented with\nverification_inputs.payment_payload.permit2_authorization.permitted.amount =\n'999999' (off-by-one tampering, e.g. via MITM or re-emission). All other\nsubset fields (owner, spender, token, nonce, deadline, signature) remain\nidentical. When the verifier recomputes binding_hash using the auditor's\npayload subset, component (b) does NOT match.\n\nVerifier MUST reject with typed reason 'binding_mismatch' and identify the\nmismatched component as 'payment_payload'. The envelope signature stays\nvalid — only the semantic binding fails.",
