  "notes": [
    "ADR-054-001: component (b) of binding hash is sha256(jcs(payment_payload_subset)) where subset is scheme-specific. For evm_permit2 the subset comprises the 8 fields enumerated in must_hash_payload_subset_fields_evm_permit2.",
    "Adversarial scenario: Permit2 amount tampered (off-by-one cent / wei). Demonstrates that binding hash binds to the EXACT authorization payload values, not to a summary or rounded representation.",
    "The tampered amount appears in two places (permit2_authorization.permitted.amount AND top-level amount) — both diverge from declared, ensuring the subset hash mismatches even if implementations differ on which field they canonicalize first.",
    "Test runner MUST recompute binding hash using verification_inputs.payment_payload (subset extraction per scheme manifest v1.0.0) and assert hash != binding_hash_declared."
  ],
